VCHIQProbe - what does RISC OS's VCHIQ module offer?
=====================================================

A first step towards hardware H.264 decoding in Reel on every Raspberry
Pi from the Pi 1 to the Pi 4. The VideoCore's H.264 decoder is reached
with MMAL, sent over VCHIQ, and RISC OS has a VCHIQ module in its ROM.
How programs are meant to call it isn't written down where we could
read it, so this finds out from the module itself.

What it does (it only reads; nothing is loaded, called or changed):
  1. asks the firmware which Pi this is;
  2. reads the VCHIQ module's header: its SWI names and numbers, its
     *commands with their syntax and help, its messages file;
  3. looks through every other module for calls to VCHIQ's SWIs, and
     lists which modules use it and which SWIs they call;
  4. saves a copy of VCHIQ and of each module that calls it in the
     Modules directory here, as Data files (so a double-click can't
     load them). They'll be taken apart to see how the calls are made.

Running it:
  Double-click Probe. A window shows the report, which is also saved as
  Result in this directory.

Please send back Result and the Modules directory (zipped). It works on
any Pi; if you have an older one (Pi 1, 2, 3 or Zero), a Result from
that too would be useful.

Needs: RISC OS 5 on a Raspberry Pi with the VCHIQ module (in the ROM).
